Package: BOAT
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Umbrella Trial Design Using Patient-Derived Organoid Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yong", "Zang", role = "aut"),
    person("Saijun", "Zhao", email = "zsj14000639@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Implements the BOAT design for randomized umbrella trials in which each patient's
    tumor gives patient-derived organoids (PDOs) that are tested with every treatment available
    in the patient's subgroup. Patient responses and PDO responses are modelled jointly, the
    response mean of each treatment is adaptively clustered across subgroups by reversible jump
    MCMC, and patients are adaptively randomized according to how well their own PDO responses
    predict clinical response. The package provides the decision boundaries, the model fit and the
    interim, final and randomization decisions needed to conduct a trial, simulation of operating
    characteristics, and calibration of the tuning parameter.
